> On 28 May 2026, at 22:01, Aditya Kousik <adityakousik@icloud.com> =
wrote:
>=20
> Hi all,
>=20
> Following up here on further discussion in code review. In the last =
design, we proposed to make all methods with a default empty body.  This =
breaks source compatibility for Scala requiring an override def.=20
>=20
> To address this, I=E2=80=99ve changed the design slightly that will =
position the improvement a bit better. I=E2=80=99ve introduced a new =
super interface RebalanceListener with exactly the same shape as =
ConsumerRebalanceListener but with the extra parameter =
RebalanceConsumer. The existing interface will simply extend it =
overriding with defaults to the 1-arg methods . We also mark =
ConsumerRebalanceListener as deprecated.
>=20
> Relatedly the set method on Consumer will be setRebalanceListener.=20
>=20
> In light of this major change, I wanted to re-open the vote so that =
everyone is onboard with the proposed changes.=20
>=20
> Do let me know your thoughts.
>=20
