I am not sure if we should apply the schedule we discussed on the other 
thread to 2025 already? Also, it's still a proposal only.

Of course, we need to find a way, assuming we adopt the proposal, to 
align to the new schedule. But I would personally rather stretch some 
releases, instead of squeezing them to get there.

We aim for 3 releases per year and we did already release 4.2 and 4.3 in 
2025. Applying the discussed schedule, would imply we release 4.4 in 
September, and 4.5 in Dec, making it 4 releases, and overall squeezing 
the release timeline. I personally don't see a need for this?

Thus, my thought was that we would only aim for 4.4 in 2025, and do 4.5 
in 2026. I am also ok to move 4.4 back by only two weeks as Bill 
proposed (KIP freeze Jun/29).

This might imply that we start the release for 4.5 late Q4/25 or early 
Q1/26, not yet taking the holiday season fully into account, and have 
the first release following the new timeline with 4.6?


Curious to hear what Omnia as RM thinks.


-Matthias


