muralibasani commented on PR #856:
URL: https://github.com/apache/kafka-site/pull/856#issuecomment-4636160595

   > I've just tried with 43 (rebasing your branch on top of markdown) and even though `generated` is only under `static` it still worked, is it expected?
   
   Yes, that's expected. It will work in both ways.
   It adds support for content/en/<v>/generated/ without removing the existing static/<v>/generated/ path.
   
   static/<v>/generated/ (old way) served by Default static → static mount
   content/en/<v>/generated/ (new way) served by the catch-all mount entry.
   
   RM can ship generated/ under either static/<v>/ or content/en/<v>/ and both work.


