Hi everyone,

Gentle nudge on this. Motivation is still a driving factor for this KIP. Spr=
ing, smallrye, micronaut (and to an extent ShareConsumers with an ack) all i=
mplement a per-record ack.=20

It would be good to support a 1P approach at the client level so users can a=
dd hooks around the scope of consuming a single record (rather than just the=
 batch as is with the current consumer interceptor). This helps cut boilerpl=
ate around instrumentation, mdc context setup etc.

Cheers,
Aditya

> On May 17, 2026, at 14:58, Aditya Kousik <adityakousik@icloud.com> wrote:
>=20
> =EF=BB=BFHi all,
>=20
> Adding on a couple more points for motivation:
>=20
> 1. Users typically set MDC context from each record but this can break in s=
ubtle ways for both sync/async threading models
>=20
> for (var r: consumer.poll(=E2=80=A6)) {
>    MDC.put(=E2=80=9Ckafka.offset=E2=80=9D, r.offset());
>    // add rest of the fields
>    process(r); // throws an ex
>    MDC.clear();
> }
>=20
> In both sync and async models, record N+1 carries prev record=E2=80=99s co=
ntext during exceptions. The solution is a try finally for cleanup, yet more=
 boilerplate for teams to maintain manually. Across thread boundaries, we ha=
ve to manually copy threadlocals around from the poller loop (such as OTel,D=
D spans).
>=20
> In KafkaShareConsumer, this behaviour is more common when worker threads c=
an perform individual redelivery, ack calls. Sometimes, a main poll loop for=
 try/catch does not neatly cleanup state between records.
>=20
> 2. I also see Confluent=E2=80=99s parallel-consumer implement a PollContex=
t to achieve a similar function to wrap each poll() action per-record.
>=20
> Best,
> Aditya
>=20
>> On Apr 16, 2026, at 11:45, Aditya Kousik <adityakousik@icloud.com> wrote:=

>>=20
>> Hi kafka dev,
>>=20
>> Gentle ping on this KIP. I=E2=80=99ve added a short [unit test reproducer=
](https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/22077) that highlights the gap mentio=
ned in the KIP.
>>=20
>> Would appreciate any eyes on both.
>>=20
>> Thanks,
>> Aditya
>>=20
>>>> On Apr 1, 2026, at 08:14, Aditya Kousik <adityakousik@icloud.com> wrote=
:
>>>=20
>>> =EF=BB=BFHi all,
>>>=20
>>> I'd like to start a discussion on KIP-1305: Per-Record Context Processin=
g for Kafka Consumers.
>>>=20
>>> https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1305%3A+Per-Record=
+Context+Processing+for+Kafka+Consumers
>>>=20
>>> Spring Kafka, SmallRye, Micronaut, OTel, and Datadog have each independe=
ntly built per-record lifecycle hooks because the client doesn't provide one=
. This KIP proposes ConsumerRecordContextProcessor, a configurable hook that=
 creates a per-record AutoCloseable context via record.newContext(), giving f=
rameworks and instrumentation libraries a single stable integration point.
>>>=20
>>> Looking forward to your feedback.
>>>=20
>>> Thanks,
>>> Aditya Kousik
>=20

