Hello Alieh,

Thanks for your comments.

AS1: Yes, that makes sense. KIP was updated. It's just a bit more
documentation so I don't think a new voting thread is needed (but I
will mention this in follow-up, though).

AS2: We allow headers to be empty, but we don't allow them to be null.
I will mention that explicitly in the documentation. Regarding
mutation, IMO I don't see a case where a user would even try to do it,
but I can mention this case as well.

KIP was updated, and the update was mentioned in the voting thread.
Let me know if you have more questions

On Tue, Jun 9, 2026 at 10:45=E2=80=AFPM Alieh Saeedi via dev
<dev@kafka.apache.org> wrote:
