Lucy Liu created KAFKA-20688:
--------------------------------

             Summary: Memory leak in RocksDBTimestampedStoreWithHeaders.ope=
nRocksDB when probing column families
                 Key: KAFKA-20688
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20688
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: streams
    Affects Versions: 4.3.0
            Reporter: Lucy Liu
             Fix For: 4.3.1


`RocksDBTimestampedStoreWithHeaders.openRocksDB(...)` allocates a `new Colu=
mnFamilyOptions()` solely to construct an `Options` for a `RocksDB.listColu=
mnFamilies(...)` probe call. The temporary `ColumnFamilyOptions` instance i=
s not referenced anywhere outside the try-with-resources block, and `Option=
s.close()` does not cascade-close the inner `ColumnFamilyOptions` in the Ro=
cksDB JNI contract. The instance is unreachable from any close path, leakin=
g one native `LRUCache` block cache per `openRocksDB` invocation. Each new =
windowed-store segment open compounds the leak.

=C2=A0

## Affected code

https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/trunk/streams/src/main/java/org/apache=
/kafka/streams/state/internals/RocksDBTimestampedStoreWithHeaders.java#L75-=
L80

```

final List<byte[]> existingCFs;
=C2=A0 try (final Options options =3D new Options(dbOptions, new ColumnFami=
lyOptions())) {
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 existingCFs =3D RocksDB.listColumnFamilies(options, db=
Dir.getAbsolutePath());
=C2=A0 } catch (final RocksDBException e) {
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 throw new ProcessorStateException("Error listing colum=
n families for store " + name, e);
=C2=A0 }

```

This path is only reached when header-aware state stores are enabled (KIP-1=
271). Workloads that do not enable that feature are unaffected.



