Hi Viktor,
Thanks for your reply. I definitely understand changing priorities :) When th=
is has more of a focus, I expect the discussion will pick up properly.

AS1: Thanks. That's clearer.

AS2: I actually quite like the idea of virtual clusters and some of this KIP =
is elegant. I'm not convinced by the binding of users to virtual clusters tho=
ugh. My concerns are firstly problem determination - it would be pretty simpl=
e to make mistakes that are hard to diagnose, and secondly that it makes the =
lifecycle management of the resources concerned a bit tricky. For example, I =
bind a user to a virtual cluster and then I delete the virtual cluster. Now w=
hat? Once the details are sorted out, it's probably a perfectly good model. A=
nyway, these are details that we're not going to resolve right now, which is =
fine.

AS3: Yes, maybe something like using the client ID to identify the principal =
for development would work. Alternatively, the client ID could be used for ol=
der clients to identify the desired virtual cluster, and have a "proper" way =
in the protocol for new clients to express their intent. For example, KIP-116=
3 suggests allows older clients to specify `diskless_rack_id=3D<rack_id>`, so=
 there is precedent.

AS4 and AS5: Yes. That's better.

AS6: This is going to be tricky. Details to be determined for sure.

Thanks,
Andrew=20

On 2026/06/04 14:37:17 Viktor Somogyi-Vass wrote:
> Hi Andrew,
>=20
> We unfortunately dropped the ball on your reply mostly because priorities
