Hi TaiJuWu,=20
Thanks for the KIP! Same worry as Luke about the per-broker size =
especially on large clusters. On top of that; this will keep growing as =
brokers get more configs over time, so we=E2=80=99d need to keep =
checking the size impact every time configs are added.=20

Thanks=20
Omnia=20

> On 15 Jun 2026, at 05:14, Luke Chen <showuon@gmail.com> wrote:
>=20
> Hi TaiJuWu,
>=20
> Thanks for the KIP.
>=20
> LC1: =46rom the rejective alternative:
> "Reporting all non-sensitive configs (~388 entries, ~18 KB per broker) =
was
> considered. While simpler in filtering logic, it includes 163 configs =
that
> have no ConfigDef validator. The additional ~8 KB per broker adds up =
in
> large clusters (8 MB for 1000 brokers) with no practical benefit =E2=80=94=
 configs
> without validators cannot be validated regardless of whether they are
> reported. The chosen approach (only configs with validators, ~225 =
entries,
> ~10 KB per broker) keeps the payload smaller and automatically expands =
when
> new validators are added in future KIPs."
>=20
> So, ~ 10 KB per broker now, and in 1000 brokers cluster, it'll be 10MB
> metadata log increase, right?
> I'm not convinced that this is necessary after reading the KIP.
> If you think 18 KB per broker is "big", then I don't know why 10 KB =
per
> broker is acceptable?
>=20
>=20
> Thanks,
> Luke
>=20
>=20
> On Thu, Jun 4, 2026 at 4:34=E2=80=AFPM TaiJu Wu <tjwu1217@gmail.com> =
wrote:
>=20
>> Hi chia:
>>=20
>> Thanks for your feedback.
>>=20
>> chia_00: I have removed this section, we don't change ConfigDef and =
add
>> test plan to cover server-side filter helper.
>> chia_01: thanks for catching this, I have updated KIP.
>> chia_02: I added following description to this KIP.
>>  If a broker reports an empty StaticConfigs, the controller should =
reject
>> the registration and prevent the broker from joining the cluster by
>> returning *INVALID_REGISTRATION*.
>>=20
>> Thanks,
>> TaiJuWu
>>=20
>>=20
>>=20
>> Chia-Ping Tsai <chia7712@apache.org> =E6=96=BC 2026=E5=B9=B46=E6=9C=881=
=E6=97=A5=E9=80=B1=E4=B8=80 =E4=B8=8A=E5=8D=8811:05=E5=AF=AB=E9=81=93=EF=BC=
=9A
>>=20
>>> chia_2: should the controller reject the request which has empty =
static
>>> configs?
>>>=20
>>> On 2026/04/30 14:47:05 TaiJu Wu wrote:
>>>> Hi all,
>>>>=20
>>>> I would like to discuss KIP-1326
>>>> <
>>>=20
>> =
https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1326%3A+Include+brok=
er+static+configurations+in+BrokerRegistrationRequest
>>>>=20
>>>> which
>>>> proposes that brokers report a subset of their static configuration
>>> values
>>>> to the controller as part of BrokerRegistrationRequest.
>>>>=20
>>>> WIKI:
>>>>=20
>>>=20
>> =
https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1326%3A+Include+brok=
er+static+configurations+in+BrokerRegistrationRequest
>>>>=20
>>>> Best,
>>>> TaiJuWu
