When share sessions are evicted or get out of sync (broker-managed), the sh=
are consumer gets=C2=A0{{{}SHARE_SESSION_NOT_FOUND{}}},=C2=A0{{{}INVALID_SH=
ARE_SESSION_EPOCH{}}}, or=C2=A0{{SHARE_SESSION_LIMIT_REACHED}}=C2=A0logged =
at INFO in=C2=A0{{{}ShareSessionHandler{}}}, with an alarming message like=
=C2=A0{{{}"Node {} was unable to process the ShareFetch/ShareAcknowledge re=
quest"{}}}.
 * This is self-healing on the client (re-sends a full ShareFetch/ShareAckn=
owledge via=C2=A0{{{}nextCloseExistingAttemptNew(){}}}); no client-side act=
ion is possible.
 * Session cache is broker-managed; visibility (metrics, configs) lives on =
the broker.
 * Broker-side logs for epoch mismatch are already at DEBUG ({{{}ShareParti=
tionManager{}}},=C2=A0{{{}ShareSessionContext{}}}).

Related:=C2=A0KAFKA-20713=C2=A0(fetch equivalent, fixed in PR #22617).

This Jira is to review the client-side log in=C2=A0{{ShareSessionHandler}}=
=C2=A0(consider DEBUG +=C2=A0{{{}isDebugEnabled{}}}, aligned with=C2=A0{{{}=
FetchSessionHandler{}}}, so apps keep relevant INFO without this noise).
