Lucas Brutschy resolved KAFKA-20624.
------------------------------------
    Resolution: Fixed

> Wire topology description plugin into GroupCoordinatorService =E2=80=94 r=
ead path (describe) and broker wiring
> -------------------------------------------------------------------------=
-----------------------------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-20624
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20624
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Sub-task
>          Components: streams
>            Reporter: Alieh Saeedi
>            Assignee: TengYao Chi
>            Priority: Major
>             Fix For: 4.4.0
>
>
> streamsGroupDescribe gains includeTopologyDescription flag. attachTopolog=
yDescriptions: call plugin.getTopology only when StoredTopologyEpoch =3D=3D=
 currentTopologyEpoch, otherwise report NOT_STORED. Status constants: NOT_R=
EQUESTED (0), NOT_STORED (1), ERROR (2), AVAILABLE (3). GroupCoordinator in=
terface update. Broker wiring: KafkaApis.scala (new handler + describe flag=
 plumbing), BrokerServer.scala (plugin instantiation + configuration), Requ=
estConvertToJson. GroupCoordinatorServiceTest (describe-path tests), KafkaA=
pisTest, RequestQuotaTest, AuthorizerIntegrationTest, checkstyle/suppressio=
ns.xml.
> Wire the streams-group topology description plugin into broker-side reque=
st
> handling, completing the KAFKA-20618 broker work that KAFKA-20620 (schema=
 +
> stubs) and KAFKA-20623 (coordinator-side write/heartbeat/delete) left for
> this ticket.
> Two paths are wired:
> 1. Describe path (read). streamsGroupDescribe is extended with an
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0IncludeTopologyDescription request flag. When the flag is se=
t and the
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0persisted StoredDescriptionTopologyEpoch matches the group's=
 current
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0topology epoch, a new StreamsGroupTopologyDescriptionManager=
.
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0attachTopologyDescriptions building block calls
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0plugin.getTopology(groupId, topologyEpoch) per group and pop=
ulates the
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0response's topology field. Each DescribedGroup carries a
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0topologyDescriptionStatus byte: NOT_REQUESTED (0) when the c=
lient did
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0not ask for it, NOT_STORED (1) when the plugin has no row at=
 the
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0requested epoch (or the epoch mismatched), ERROR (2) when th=
e plugin
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0call failed, AVAILABLE (3) when the topology is attached. Ch=
ain
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0assembly lives on GroupCoordinatorService.streamsGroupDescri=
be; the
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0manager exposes per-group plugin invocation as a building bl=
ock
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0(mirroring invokeSetTopology / invokeDeleteTopologies).
> 2. Update path (write =E2=80=94 KafkaApis wiring).
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0KafkaApis.handleStreamsGroupTopologyDescriptionUpdate curren=
tly lives as
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0a placeholder stub that always returns UNSUPPORTED_VERSION (=
scaffolding
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0from KAFKA-20620). Replace it with the real handler: gate on
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0isStreamsGroupProtocolEnabled (returns UNSUPPORTED_VERSION w=
hen the
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0streams group protocol is disabled), authorize READ on GROUP=
 for the
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0request's groupId (returns GROUP_AUTHORIZATION_FAILED if den=
ied =E2=80=94 per
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0KIP-1331, "like offset commits, we don't consider this a mod=
ification
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0of the GROUP, which allows deploying apps with READ ACLs"), =
then call
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0groupCoordinator.streamsGroupTopologyDescriptionUpdate(...) =
and send
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0the result via requestHelper.sendMaybeThrottle. Same shape a=
s the
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0sibling handleStreamsGroupHeartbeat. The coordinator-side me=
thod was
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0added in KAFKA-20623 split 2 (#22552); only the KafkaApis si=
de is
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0missing =E2=80=94 flagged on the split 2 review.
> Broker wiring (shared). BrokerServer.scala instantiates the plugin via
> config.getConfiguredInstance(...) and threads it into the
> GroupCoordinatorService builder (verify the describe path doesn't need
> additional wiring beyond what KAFKA-20623 already added).
> RequestConvertToJson adds entries for StreamsGroupTopologyDescriptionUpda=
te
> Request/Response and for the new topology-description fields on the
> describe response so request/response logging tools can render them.



