Hello Jun, chia,

Thanks for your feedback.

JR3 JR4 I have updated the KIP.

JR2 The new-partition detection mechanism is reusable. The coordinator =
already has=20
access to both timestamps required for classification, so the =
determination can be made=20
server-side without introducing any new RPCs. The main difference is =
where the policy is=20
enforced: modern consumer resolves it on the client, whereas a share =
group resolves the=20
starting offset on the partition leader. As a result, the classification =
decision would need to=20
be propagated through the existing share-state initialization path. We =
would also need to persist=20
the group's creation time as part of the share-group state, since that =
information is not stored today.=20

None of this is a blocker, but it does require changes to the =
share-state format and introduces=20
a share-specific configuration. Given that additional scope, I would =
prefer to keep share groups out=20
of scope for this KIP and address them in a follow-up effort, while =
documenting the relevant reuse=20
opportunities here.

