Shekhar Prasad Rajak created KAFKA-20738:
--------------------------------------------

             Summary:  Producer 2PC init sets v6-only InitProducerId fields=
 but request builder caps version at v5
                 Key: KAFKA-20738
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20738
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: core
    Affects Versions: 4.2.1
            Reporter: Shekhar Prasad Rajak
            Assignee: Shekhar Prasad Rajak
             Fix For: 4.3.0


Kafka producer exposes transaction.two.phase.commit.enable=3Dtrue, but a pr=
oducer cannot currently initialize a 2PC transaction through the public API=
. TransactionManager sets Enable2Pc=3Dtrue in
=C2=A0 InitProducerIdRequestData, which is only valid in InitProducerId v6.=
 However, InitProducerIdRequest.Builder is constructed with the default sta=
ble-version range, so NetworkClient selects v5 and serialization
=C2=A0 fails.

=C2=A0 Example:

=C2=A0 Properties props =3D new Properties();
=C2=A0 props.put(ProducerConfig.BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS_CONFIG, bootstrap);
=C2=A0 props.put(ProducerConfig.TRANSACTIONAL_ID_CONFIG, "txn-2pc");
=C2=A0 props.put(ProducerConfig.ENABLE_IDEMPOTENCE_CONFIG, "true");
=C2=A0 props.put(ProducerConfig.TRANSACTION_TWO_PHASE_COMMIT_ENABLE_CONFIG,=
 "true");

=C2=A0 KafkaProducer<byte[], byte[]> producer =3D new KafkaProducer<>(props=
);
=C2=A0 producer.initTransactions();

=C2=A0 Current behavior:

=C2=A0 UnsupportedVersionException:
=C2=A0 Attempted to write a non-default enable2Pc at version 5

=C2=A0

so here :=C2=A0

=C2=A0

KafkaProducer
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 -> TransactionManager.initializeTransactions()
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 -> InitProducerIdRequestData.setEnable2Pc(true)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 -> new InitProducerIdRequest.Builder(data)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 -> AbstractRequest.Builder(ApiKeys.INIT_PRODUCER_ID) allows s=
table versions only
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 -> NetworkClient selects InitProducerId v5
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 -> serialization fails because Enable2Pc is v6-only

=C2=A0

=C2=A0

Expected behavior:

=C2=A0 When Enable2Pc or KeepPreparedTxn is set, the InitProducerId builder=
 should allow v6. NetworkClient should then select v6 if the broker adverti=
ses it through ApiVersions. If the broker does not support v6, the
=C2=A0 producer should fail cleanly with a clear unsupported-version error.



