Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-20739) Transaction coordinator rejects
 InitProducerId v6 recovery with KeepPreparedTxn=true
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Shekhar Prasad Rajak (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Shekhar Prasad Rajak created KAFKA-20739:
--------------------------------------------

             Summary: Transaction coordinator rejects InitProducerId v6 rec=
overy with KeepPreparedTxn=3Dtrue
                 Key: KAFKA-20739
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20739
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: core
    Affects Versions: 4.2.1
            Reporter: Shekhar Prasad Rajak
             Fix For: 4.3.1


InitProducerId v6 defines KeepPreparedTxn, OngoingTxnProducerId, and Ongoin=
gTxnProducerEpoch for 2PC recovery. Even when InitProducerId v6 is forced d=
irectly and broker-side 2PC is enabled, the transaction
=C2=A0 coordinator rejects keepPreparedTxn=3Dtrue with UNSUPPORTED_VERSION.

=C2=A0 Example:

=C2=A0 InitProducerIdRequestData data =3D new InitProducerIdRequestData()
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 .setTransactionalId("txn-2pc")
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 .setTransactionTimeoutMs(10)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 .setProducerId(RecordBatch.NO_PRODUCER_ID)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 .setProducerEpoch(RecordBatch.NO_PRODUCER_EPOCH)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 .setEnable2Pc(true)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 .setKeepPreparedTxn(true);

=C2=A0 InitProducerIdRequest request =3D
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 new InitProducerIdRequest.Builder(data).build((short) =
6);

=C2=A0 Current behavior:

=C2=A0 errorCode =3D 35

=C2=A0 35 is Errors.UNSUPPORTED_VERSION.

=C2=A0 Flow:

=C2=A0 InitProducerId v6 request
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 -> KafkaApis.handleInitProducerIdRequest()
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 -> TransactionCoordinator.handleInitProducerId()
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 -> keepPreparedTxn =3D=3D true
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 -> returns Errors.UNSUPPORTED_VERSION

=C2=A0 Expected behavior:

=C2=A0 With broker config transaction.two.phase.commit.enable=3Dtrue, keepP=
reparedTxn=3Dtrue should be accepted when enable2Pc=3Dtrue.

=C2=A0 If there is no ongoing 2PC transaction:

=C2=A0 error =3D NONE
=C2=A0 ongoingTxnProducerId =3D -1
=C2=A0 ongoingTxnProducerEpoch =3D -1

=C2=A0 If there is an ongoing 2PC transaction:

=C2=A0 error =3D NONE
=C2=A0 broker preserves the ongoing transaction
=C2=A0 response includes ongoingTxnProducerId / ongoingTxnProducerEpoch
=C2=A0 client enters PREPARED_TRANSACTION
=C2=A0 completeTransaction(preparedTxnState) can finalize it

=C2=A0

=C2=A0

=C2=A0 Expected broker/client state flow:

=C2=A0 Client: =C2=A0READY -> IN_TRANSACTION -> PREPARED_TRANSACTION
=C2=A0 Broker: =C2=A0EMPTY -> ONGOING 2PC transaction
=C2=A0 Crash/restart
=C2=A0 Client: =C2=A0initTransactions(true)
=C2=A0 Broker: =C2=A0returns ongoing producer id/epoch
=C2=A0 Client: =C2=A0PREPARED_TRANSACTION
=C2=A0 Client: =C2=A0completeTransaction(preparedState)
=C2=A0 Broker: =C2=A0PREPARE_COMMIT -> COMPLETE_COMMIT

=C2=A0



