Hi Jun,
When a user adds an existing topic to a share group subscription, we do use t=
he auto.offset.reset policy because those partitions already exist and may we=
ll have data on them. We only use 0 in the case where a topic already being c=
onsumed gained some additional new partitions. These partitions will be empty=
 at the time of creation, so zero seems like a reasonable starting point. Par=
titions being consumed in a share group always have a known starting position=
 once assigned. We don't have the equivalent of a consumer group not having a=
 committed offset.

