Hello all,

The metadata blindness and consumer downtime windows are inherently=20
unpredictable, making a fixed by_duration approach unviable. No static=20=

duration can accommodate both extremes:=20

- Short durations fail during extended downtimes, leading to the exact =
silent data=20
loss this KIP aims to prevent.=20
- Long durations (calibrated for worst-case scenarios) cause routine =
restarts to=20
trigger unnecessary mass replays, undermining the latest offset reset =
policy.=20

This is why the proposed solution uses creation time. It provides a =
discrete,=20
deterministic signal=E2=80=94verifying whether a partition is actually =
newer than the group,=20
rather than relying on an arbitrary time window that has no correlation =
with the consumer=E2=80=99s=20
actual downtime.

Best Regards,
